  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\n\nA mid level shortwave passing thru the Great Lakes this morning\nwill help carve out a larger scale trough across the eastern US.\nThis will result in a northwest flow pattern across the Ohio Valley. \nAt the surface a weak cold front will pass thru ILN/s FA this\nevening. The air mass has very limited moisture - so no pcpn is\nexpected. \n\nA modest drop in temperatures will follow for a couple of days as \nsurface high pressure of Canadian origin builds in from the \nnorthwest behind the front. This high departs to the east by midweek \nand allows for returning southerly flow and somewhat warmer air.\n\nAnother cold front will push into the area later Wednesday into\nThursday. However, moisture will still be limited, so rain is not\nexpected. \n\nModel solutions indicating a warm up late in the week into next \nweekend as a mid level ridge builds into the region. Rain chances\nincrease for the second half of next weekend as a system approaches\nfrom the south.",
